  <section class="faq-section"> <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <!-- analytics:faq-injected faq-id=faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-1 -->
      <details data-faq data-faq-id="faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-1"> <summary>How many dispensaries currently operate in Sanford?</summary> <p>Two to three licensed adult-use dispensaries currently operate in Sanford. This is a low density for a city of 21,000 residents plus a regional draw from York County towns. The effective market (Sanford residents plus regional customers) is approximately 40,000-50,000 people.</p> </details> <!-- analytics:faq-injected faq-id=faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-2 -->
      <details data-faq data-faq-id="faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-2"> <summary>What is the local licensing fee for a Sanford cannabis dispensary?</summary> <p>The City of Sanford charges $2,000-$2,500 annually for a local cannabis retail license, depending on the license type and size. Combined with <a href="/guides/maine-dispensary-license">Maine OCP</a> state license fees ($500-$1,500 annually), total annual licensing costs are approximately $2,500-$4,000.</p> </details> <!-- analytics:faq-injected faq-id=faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-3 -->
      <details data-faq data-faq-id="faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-3"> <summary>Can I capture New Hampshire customers in Sanford?</summary> <p>Yes. Southern New Hampshire (Dover, Rochester, Somersworth) has limited dispensary options and higher prices than Maine. A Sanford dispensary is closer and more convenient for these customers than Portland. Cross-border traffic is a meaningful revenue driver for well-located Sanford stores.</p> </details> <!-- analytics:faq-injected faq-id=faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-4 -->
      <details data-faq data-faq-id="faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-4"> <summary>What is the best location strategy for Sanford?</summary> <p>Route 109 / Main Street has the highest traffic and visibility. The I-95 Exit 19 area captures highway travelers and NH crossover customers. Route 11 in western Sanford serves residential neighborhoods at lower rent with community-focused positioning.</p> </details> <!-- analytics:faq-injected faq-id=faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-5 -->
      <details data-faq data-faq-id="faq-guides--sanford-dispensary-guide--s1-5"> <summary>What <a href="/guides/maine-dispensary-costs">startup investment</a> is required for a Sanford dispensary?</summary> <p>Total <a href="/guides/maine-dispensary-costs">startup investment</a> is $150,000-$300,000 including buildout ($100,000-$200,000), opening inventory ($25,000-$50,000), licensing fees ($2,500-$4,000), and working capital. Annual operating costs run $120,000-$220,000 for rent, staff, security, and utilities.</p> </details> </section> <section class="related-guides"> <h2>Related Guides</h2> <p>Explore related content for your Maine cannabis operation:</p> <ul> <li><a >Biddeford Guide →</a></li> <li><a >Portland Guide →</a></li> <li><a >South Portland Guide →</a></li> </ul> </section> <section class="further-reading"> <h2>External Resources</h2> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/adult-use" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maine Office of Cannabis Policy (OCP) — Adult Use</a></li> <li>City of Sanford Official Website</li><li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/sos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maine Secretary of State — Cannabis Resources</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/sanfordtownmaine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Census Bureau — Sanford, Maine</a></li> </ul> </section> <section class="disclaimer"> <p><em>Informational only. Verify current local fees and <a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-zoning-requirements">zoning</a> with the City of Sanford before pursuing any cannabis business. Business projections are estimates based on comparable Maine markets.</em></p> </section> 
